[?2004h[01;32mappuser@8bef2e9355c8[00m:[01;34m/app[00m$ echo "===== input/original_instruction.md ====="; cat -n input/original_instruction.md
[?2004l===== input/original_instruction.md =====
     1	# Original instruction — the client's first message
     2	
     3	I am Delphine Marr. What follows is what I asked for to begin with, one entry per subject. The subject shown on each entry is the value the draft's `subject` column uses.
     4	
     5	## OI-201 `addressee`
     6	
     7	Address the letter to the father's attorney.
     8	
     9	## OI-202 `right_of_first_refusal`
    10	
    11	Say that Mr Adler — the father — agreed to a right of first refusal, and that the children are not to be left overnight without him present. Both the agreement and the overnight restriction must appear.
    12	
    13	## OI-203 `children_named`
    14	
    15	Name both children with their ages: Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve. Both names and both ages are required.
    16	
    17	## OI-204 `overnight_stays`
    18	
    19	State that on several occasions both children stayed overnight at her home or with a sitter while the father was away — both places must be mentioned, both children, and several occasions.
    20	
    21	## OI-205 `inconsistent_accounts`
    22	
    23	Note that the father has called her his wife to the school, the person the child lives with to clinicians, a sitter to me, and his partner to the neighbours. All four audiences are required.
    24	
    25	## OI-206 `concern`
    26	
    27	Say I am concerned she may not appreciate that the stays violate the order or the position she has been put in — both limbs. (Superseded wherever the clarification speaks to concern.)
    28	
    29	## OI-207 `behavioural_plan`
    30	
    31	Say the behavioural plan is about confidence and stability and the stays have set it back — confidence, stability, and setback all required. (Superseded wherever the clarification speaks to behavioural_plan.)
    32	
    33	## OI-208 `request`
    34	
    35	Ask that neither child remain overnight in her care unless the father is present.
    36	
    37	## OI-209 `enclosure`
    38	
    39	Say a certified copy of the custodial plan is enclosed.
    40	
    41	## OI-210 `tone`
    42	
    43	Keep it soft, formal and succinct — all three. (Superseded wherever the clarification speaks to tone.)
    44	
    45	## OI-211 `sender_signature`
    46	
    47	Sign it in my own name as Delphine Marr — the full name is required; do not sign as counsel or on behalf of anyone else.
